# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# xNPV Model .gitignore
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. Two rules carry the weight here:
#   1. Nothing confidential or machine-specific goes in.
#   2. 30_OUTPUT regenerates from code, so it never gets committed.
#
# 10_SOURCE uses an allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include the four
# small vendor CSVs that were explicitly approved for commit. The hard deny
# on *CONFIDENTIAL* sits at the very bottom because git applies last-match-
# wins, so nothing above it can accidentally re-include those files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets and machine-specific config ---
.env
.env.local
.claude/

# --- Generated output. Regenerable from code, drifts every run ---
30_OUTPUT/
Work/
90_ARCHIVE/

# --- Source data: ignore everything by default ---
10_SOURCE/*

# ...then re-include only the four approved vendor CSVs.
# These are third-party licensed data (TopDownHockey / hockeystats).
# See 10_SOURCE/README.md for provenance and attribution.
!10_SOURCE/WAR.csv
!10_SOURCE/Goalies_WAR.csv
!10_SOURCE/nhle_temporal.csv
!10_SOURCE/draft_slot_baseline.csv
!10_SOURCE/README.md

# --- Databases and large binaries, wherever they appear ---
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.zip

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS and editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# --- Sync-conflict copies. These have bitten this project before:
#     "aging_curve (1).py", "age_join (2).py" and nine others were found
#     in a stale competing script set during the 2026-07-30 audit. ---
*conflicted copy*
* (1).*
* (2).*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HARD DENY. Must remain the last matching rule in this file.
# The PuckPedia player and trades exports are confidential vendor data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*CONFIDENTIAL*
